@startuml launch
!theme plain
title Starting an executor under an agent account through the launcher

participant "Dispatcher\n(unprivileged, configured caller)" as D
participant "sudo" as S
participant "swarma-user-launcher\n(root, no arguments)" as L
database "Ledger + policy\n(root-owned)" as R
participant "Executor\n(agent account, uid 612)" as E
participant "Broker" as B

D -> D: close broker connections (no descriptor may cross)
D -> S: sudo /opt/swarma/libexec/swarma-user-launcher\n(stdin: launch-op/1 {generation, execution_id, epoch, executor, plan})
S -> L: exec as root (SUDO_UID = dispatcher)
L -> R: shared lock; g-0193 active, kind agent, created by this dispatcher?
L -> R: executor id → approved path + SHA-256
L -> L: open the executable without following links; verify the digest
L -> L: start receipt; setsid; home as cwd
L -> L: close descriptors > 2; plan → pipe → descriptor 3;\nfixed environment; clear groups; set GID, UID; root cannot be regained
L -> E: exec the verified executor as uid 612
E -> E: read the plan; resolve the protected credential binding
E -> B: fresh connection; lease.request (broker lease-at-launch)
note over S, E: sudo stays the parent and relays signals:\nthe dispatcher owns the process lifetime
@enduml
